SUMMARY:Josh Johnson's Comedy Band Camp LIVE at Kingsbury Hall (Fri)
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout Josh Johnson\nJosh Johnson is one of the most exciting and intellectually sharp comedians working today. With over 10 million followers across social media\, he was recently called “the funniest guy on the internet” by WIRED. An Emmy-nominated writer\, stand-up comedian\, actor\, and NAACP award-winner from Louisiana by way of Chicago\, Johnson is currently a rotating host and correspondent on Comedy Central’s Emmy & Peabody Award-winning program The Daily Show. \nJohnson is a prolific creator who releases weekly stand-up sets on his YouTube channel — content that has been viewed over half a billion times worldwide. In 2025 alone\, he released 38 hours of topical stand-up material performed in front of live audiences. His comedy is intelligent\, timely\, and deeply human — the kind that makes you laugh and think at the same time. \nThe Comedy Band Camp is Josh’s most ambitious live show yet — a unique\, immersive comedy experience that he describes as “the camp experience he never had\, so he made it for you.” This is not your typical stand-up show. \nEvent Details\nDate: Friday\, August 21\, 2026 \nTime: 7:00 PM MDT \nVenue: Kingsbury Hall\, 1395 Presidents Circle\, Salt Lake City\, UT 84112 \nPhone: (801) 581-7100 \nNote: A Saturday night show (Aug 22 at 8:30 PM) is also available. See separate listing. \nAbout Kingsbury Hall\nKingsbury Hall is one of Salt Lake City’s most beloved and historic performance venues\, located on the campus of the University of Utah at 1395 Presidents Circle. With a seating capacity of approximately 1\,900\, it offers an intimate yet grand atmosphere perfect for a show as unique as Comedy Band Camp. \nThe hall features excellent sightlines from virtually every seat\, outstanding acoustics\, and a warm\, welcoming ambiance. Managed by UtahPresents\, Kingsbury Hall has hosted world-class performers across comedy\, music\, and theater for decades. Parking is available in nearby University of Utah parking structures\, and the venue is accessible via TRAX light rail. \nWhat to Expect\nJosh Johnson’s Comedy Band Camp is unlike any comedy show you’ve seen before. Blending stand-up\, performance art\, and interactive elements\, the show creates a fully immersive experience that has been wowing audiences across the country. Expect opening acts\, dancers (the famous Flower Girls)\, and Josh’s signature brand of intelligent\, topical humor. \nJosh is known for crafting material that is specific to the current moment — so every show feels fresh and relevant. His ability to weave together serious topics with genuine hilarity is unmatched in comedy right now. Fans consistently describe his shows as life-changing experiences. \nDoors open approximately 45 minutes before showtime. Arrive early to find your seats and soak in the Kingsbury Hall atmosphere. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: Check venue for current pricing \nTickets are available through the official Kingsbury Hall box office and authorized resale platforms. Both Friday and Saturday shows are available — check both listings! \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/josh-johnsons-comedy-band-camp-live-at-kingsbury-hall-fri/
LOCATION:Kingsbury Hall Salt Lake City\, 1395 Presidents Circle\, Salt Lake City\, Utah\, 84112\, United States
